@start **The window opens on a single spine column.** Column 0, `chaB`, is carried by 100% of chromosomes, persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0% of calls {S1}. The model names 98% of them, at 0.10 bits {S1}.

@variable **The first fork is at `chaA`**, column 1, carried by 89%, with `chaC` in 11% {S2.c1}. The `dha` genes, columns 19 to 22, are [[dihydroxyacetone kinase]] {S2.c19-22, Q}. A branch of 16 persistent families runs through columns 5 to 20 in 11%, [[nitrate reduction and respiration]] {S2.b5}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine column than on the fork and variable ones**, 98% against 91%, and hesitates less there, 0.10 against 0.48 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 54, `ariR`, a fork column, 1.10 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends in the `pot` genes**, columns 73 to 78, [[spermidine and putrescine transport]] {S2.c73-78, Q}. The last column is `ycfZ`, in 29% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 91% of genes**, 0.48 bits on average, perplexity 1.6 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.24 against 0.25 bits, and names fewer genes, 77% against 96% {C}.

